ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 32910, Sep. 20, 2022>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 18 (4), 25 (1) 5, and (3) shall enter into force on January 1, 2023.
Article 2 (General applicability)
This Decree shall begin to apply where a tender announcement is made or negotiated contracts are executed after this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to two-stage bidding)
The amended provisions of Article 18 (4) shall begin to apply where a tender announcements made for two-stage bidding under Article 18 (1) or (3) after the enforcement date under the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda.
Article 4 (Transitional measure concerning execution of negotiated contracts)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 25 (3), the previous provisions of Article 25 (3) shall apply where procedures for executing a negotiated contract are underway pursuant to the previous provisions of Article 25 (3) as at the enforcement date under the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning criteria for examining abilities for performing contracts)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 42 (4) through (6), the previous provisions of Article 42 (4) shall apply where the Mayor/Do Governor is under consultation with the Minister of the Interior and Safety pursuant to the previous provisions of Article 42 (4) regarding the criteria for examining the ability to perform contracts as at the time this Decree enters into force.

